  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 208 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nEarly to mid week, upper troughing will persist across the\nwestern U.S. with a closed low of the coast of southern\nCalifornia by Wednesday. Upper ridging will amplify across the\nCentral U.S. Weak disturbances from the Desert Southwest into\nthe CentraL Plains will bring some increase in clouds. Isolated\nrain showers cannot be ruled out Monday night through \nWednesday, though the current forecast remains dry. Highs in the\n60s Monday warm into the 70s by Wednesday. \n\nBy Thursday and Friday, the western US upper trough/closed low \nwill advance east across the Rockies by late Friday, bringing a\nreturn of southwesterly flow aloft. At the surface, low \npressure will begin to eject across the Dakotas by Friday \nevening, and this drags a cold front into the area sometime \nSaturday. This will bring continued highs in the 70s Thursday\nand Friday. Some threat for precipitation as well Thursday night\ninto next weekend, and this will need to be monitored as the\ncold front interacts will some increase in Gulf moisture.",
